menu "Morse Micro Shim Configuration"
    config MM_RESET_N
        int "RESET_N pin for MM chip"
        default -1
        help
            Output gpio pin used to control the RESET_N line.

    config MM_RESET_SETTLE_MS
        int "Delay after releasing RESET_N, in milliseconds"
        default 20
        range 1 1000
        help
            Delay between releasing RESET_N and the first SPI clocking. This must cover the
            transceiver's boot, not just its reset pulse.

            The startup handshake clocks a training sequence and then polls for the command
            response. A transceiver that is still booting when that clocking starts can latch
            onto a bit phase that is not byte aligned with the host's framing and hold it for
            the rest of the boot, so the handshake reads a correct response at the wrong
            alignment and the driver rejects it as an invalid ack. The failure is intermittent
            and looks like absent or faulty hardware.

            Adjust this based on the boot time measured on your particular board to ensure
            that the transceiver has sufficient time to boot.

    config MM_WAKE
        int "WAKE pin for MM chip"
        default -1
        help
            Output gpio pin used to control the WAKE line.

    config MM_BUSY
        int "BUSY pin for the MM chip"
        default -1
        help
            Input pin used as a rising edge interrupt.

    config MM_SPI_SCK
        int "SCK pin for MM chip"
        default -1
        help
            SPI clock pin.

    config MM_SPI_MOSI
        int "MOSI pin for MM chip"
        default -1
        help
            SPI master out slave in pin.

    config MM_SPI_MISO
        int "MISO pin for MM chip"
        default -1
        help
            SPI master in slave out pin.

    config MM_SPI_CS
        int "SPI CS pin for MM chip"
        default -1
        help
            SPI chip select pin.

    config MM_SPI_IRQ
        int "SPI IRQ pin for MM chip"
        default -1
        help
            Out of band interupt pin used to indicate that
            the MM chip has data for the host.

    config MM_SPI_CLOCK_MHZ
        int "SPI clock for MM chip (MHz)"
        range 1 50
        default 40
        help
            Requested SPI clock. The MM chip allows up to 50 MHz, but the ESP SPI clock is
            divided from an 80 MHz source, so 40 MHz is the highest exact value; the driver
            rounds other values to the nearest frequency it can produce.

    config MM_SPI_FAST_PATH
        bool "Drive the SPI peripheral directly for MM chip transfers"
        default y
        help
            The SDIO-over-SPI protocol makes many single-byte transfers per packet (bus ready
            polls, tokens, CRC bytes). Through the ESP-IDF SPI master driver each of them is a
            complete driver transaction (bus lock, DMA set-up, start, wait), which is much
            longer than the byte itself and limits throughput.

            With this option the driver only configures the bus and device once; every
            transfer then writes the SPI data registers directly (CPU mode, up to 64 bytes per
            hardware transfer, longer buffers in 64-byte chunks) and polls for completion, as
            the mm-iot-sdk STM32 platforms do. Chip select is a GPIO driven by morselib, so the
            chunking is not visible to the MM chip. Disable to use the SPI master driver for
            every transfer.

endmenu
